# This is a single-file game: all artwork ships embedded as data URIs inside
# index.html, so the repo never needs loose image files. Ignore every image so
# debug screenshots, source art, and reference shots can't get pushed by accident.
# (If you ever genuinely need to commit one, use: git add -f <file>)
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.gif
*.webp
*.bmp

# reference screenshots from the original game (not ours to publish) — kept
# explicit for documentation; already covered by the rules above
example.png
p1demo.png
bug1.png
bug-again.png

# Working files, not deliverables. The two big ones matter: a saved copy of
# index.html is ~1.2 MB, and git keeps every blob forever — a handful of those
# would outweigh the entire rest of the repo. Any version you need is already
# reachable from history, so save snapshots here rather than committing them.
# multi-agent coordination board
.aihive/
# plans, one-off harnesses, design handoffs
.scratch/
# saved builds of index.html for side-by-side testing
test-*.html
